// std/task/decorators: what the primitives of this module are to the task check.
//
// The body of a primitive shares a task's state with the threads of the scheduler,
// which no task may race on: the task check reads its decorator instead of its body.
// What a primitive does is a contract of the runtime, not a property of its code
// (`locked` runs its body alone only because the scheduler never preempts it), so it
// is said where the primitive is declared. Both decorators are private: no other
// module can claim to be a primitive.
//
// A field names a parameter of the primitive, or a field of the struct the primitive
// is lent first, by its name; `""` names none. The check stops the compiler on a name
// that does not exist, and reads the values as written, so each one is a literal.

module "std/task"

/// What the function below is to a task. A primitive with no field given does
/// nothing to a task that the check could see.
task_primitive :: decorator(.Function) {
    /// The parameter holding the fn a task runs.
    runs: string = ""
    /// The parameter holding a value handed on to other tasks, which may do anything
    /// with it.
    gives: string = ""
    /// The parameter holding the task whose end the call waits for, or the array of
    /// tasks each of which it waits for. Each task holds what it returned in its field
    /// `result`.
    joins: string = ""
    /// The parameter holding the fn run holding a lock, handed the value `guards`
    /// names.
    exclusive: string = ""
    /// The call may park the task that makes it.
    parks: bool = false
    /// The field the call assigns.
    writes: string = ""
    /// The array field the call grows.
    grows: string = ""
    /// The call returns a value another task handed on, which belongs to the caller
    /// from then on.
    takes: bool = false
    /// The field the lock guards.
    guards: string = ""
}

/// The struct below is shared by design: every task holding one reaches the same
/// value, which the task check does not race and a deep copy keeps instead of
/// copying.
task_shared :: decorator(.Struct) {}
